From 1a7eaad218ab64f9e3f24173754d568994753491 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:50:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] Add Prettier and ESLint 10 (config only)

- Prettier 3 with prettier-plugin-tailwindcss: single quotes, no semicolons, 100 columns, Tailwind
  v4 class order (globals.css) inside className, cn() and cva(). `pnpm format` / `format:check`.
- ESLint 10 flat config (eslint/config defineConfig): @eslint/js, typescript-eslint
  strictTypeChecked + stylisticTypeChecked with the project service, react-hooks 7 (with the React
  Compiler rules), @eslint-react recommended-type-checked, jsx-a11y, react-refresh (vite),
  simple-import-sort, eslint-config-prettier last. Named exports only in src/.
- Type-aware linting needs TypeScript's JS API, which TS 7 doesn't ship yet: `typescript` is the
  TS 6 compatibility package for tools and `tsc` stays TS 7 (`@typescript/native`), as the
  TypeScript team recommends for running both side by side.
- The root tsconfig.json is now a solution (app, storybook, tests) so the project service finds
  every file; `pnpm typecheck` is `tsc -b`.
- CI runs format:check and lint before the type check. VS Code: format on save, ESLint fixes on
  save, recommended extensions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Te9bARZBkSfcxCSZLhK4ZW
